presentations/week_9/ac19-cascade-week-9.html
results/heuristic_search/ac19_autmin_10k_smoke/

# The 1,000-node arm comparison over the whole aut-min screen: 41 MB of raw
# jsonl per arm, and this repo's own pattern (see ac19_autmin_screen/) commits
# the DERIVED costs and the residues rather than the screen. ac19_s40_1k_costs.csv
# and RESULTS.md carry everything the deck and the argument read; the jsonl is
# regenerated by run_ac19_cascade_screen with --arm s40_gen / s20_bare.
# ... but the DATA IS PUSHED, gzipped. 90 MB of raw jsonl compresses to 6.6 MB
# (14:1 and 20:1 -- the records are highly repetitive), which is small enough to
# track and complete enough that nothing has to be re-run to check a claim. The
# whole reason ac19_autmin_10k exists is that a previous wave's per-row data was
# never committed and could not be recovered; the lesson is to commit it, not to
# commit less of it.
results/heuristic_search/ac19_s40_1k/ac19_cascade_screen_*.jsonl
!results/heuristic_search/ac19_s40_1k/ac19_cascade_screen_*.jsonl.gz
